STEP 2 -- THE BOUNDARY ANNULUS for any j with no certified safe-zone zero
==============================================================================
  first j with no safe-zone zero : 7
  winding DIFFERENCE D(r) = w(F_S,r) - w(F_Euler,r) in the annulus:
     j = 7   D(0.96) = 7  D(0.97) = 0  D(0.98) = 2  D(0.99) = -2
     j = 8   D(0.96) = -2  D(0.97) = -1  D(0.98) = 3  D(0.99) = 6
     j = 9   D(0.96) = -2  D(0.97) = -34  D(0.98) = 2  D(0.99) = 4
     j = 10  D(0.96) = -2  D(0.97) = -16  D(0.98) = 3  D(0.99) = -8
     j = 11  D(0.96) = -2  D(0.97) = -26  D(0.98) = 4  D(0.99) = -2
     j = 12  D(0.96) = -2  D(0.97) = -26  D(0.98) = -7  D(0.99) = 18

  D(r) >= 1 anywhere  => the zero merely moved into the annulus, Theorem A
                         survives (the safe zone was just too small).
  D(r) = 0 for all r  => a genuine COUNTEREXAMPLE to Theorem A's hard half:
                         F_S zero-free in the disk with S non-empty.

